#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:5
#: e254935ff9c34945a71251007db811b5
msgid "Intel Aero RTF"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:10
#: 4f4ca2ea3f3740a68ab6229033d7b67e
msgid "The `Intel Aero RTF vehicle <https://software.intel.com/en-us/aero/drone-kit>`__ includes the :ref:`Intel Aero compute board <common-intel-aero-overview>`, `Vision Accessory Kit <https://software.intel.com/en-us/aero/vision-kit>`__ and a `Spektrum DXe transmitter <http://spektrumrc.com/Products/Default.aspx?ProdId=SPM1000>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:13
#: bd48051eeafd4bfc9068517022e3e516
msgid "Within the vehicle is an STM32F427V autopilot board which can run ArduPilot (replacing the pre-loaded non-ArduPilot software). In this way, the higher powered :ref:`Intel Aero compute board <common-intel-aero-overview>` is used as a `companion computer <https://ardupilot.org/dev/docs/companion-computers.html>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:20
#: 2ebdfaab9913499e87a13ef9beab1a47
msgid "Additional parts to buy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:22
#: 6fa0cf1904fc4ba1ac3c7d10fb853785
msgid "Although \"Ready-to-fly\" some additional parts are required to complete the upgrade and fly with ArduPilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:24
#: da14c19ba2cd4832a8c7e127b2976c5f
msgid "LiPo battery `3S <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/multistar-high-capacity-3s-5200mah-multi-rotor-lipo-pack.html?___store=en_us>`__ or `4S <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/multistar-high-capacity-5200mah-4s-12c-multi-rotor-lipo-pack-w-xt60.html?___store=en_us>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:25
#: 43cff98acaed4e8f91670c49d2c8a608
msgid "2GB (or larger) USB thumb drive (`like this one <https://www.amazon.com/SanDisk-Cruzer-Glide-Drive-SDCZ60-008G-B35/dp/B007YX9O94/ref=sr_1_4?ie=UTF8&qid=1492397331&sr=8-4>`__) is needed for updating to the last release of the Linux distro."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:26
#: 518d30597c3c4f6daa6c8e4c4ad22df8
msgid "Micro USB OTG to USB cable (`like this one <https://www.amazon.com/Micro-USB-OTG-Go-Adapter/dp/B005GI2VMG>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:27
#: e59e3cb5ac3b4600b564bb2f97b1e554
msgid "`Spektrum USB programming cable <https://www.spektrumrc.com/Products/Default.aspx?ProdID=SPMA3065>`__ (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:30
#: 14f396830dcc4980852dff9ff0859f43
msgid "Upgrading the vehicle's software"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:32
#: 5f18cdc3aeba4895ab295842d3bbb3b4
msgid "The Aero RTF may not have the last BIOS and Linux operating system. The Linux distro on Aero needs to be updated to version 1.2 in order for the autopilot to be flashed with ArduPilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:35
#: af4447fb8c8a4ec283d4c6eb1fd20106
msgid "`Official Setup Instructions from Intel <https://github.com/intel-aero/meta-intel-aero/wiki/02-Initial-setup>`__ should be followed which will ask you to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:37
#: c0caa8b5cbfb4a258c259e870d7788fc
msgid "Download the latest OS image (aka \"intel-aero-image-intel-aero.iso\") and Capsule/BIOS (aka \"capsule-01.00.12-r0.core2_64.rpm\") from the `Intel Download Center <https://downloadcenter.intel.com/download/26500/UAV-installation-files-for-Intel-Aero-Platform>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:38
#: 2c1f5cae8786400e9ab16b2171e50abe
msgid "`Flash the BIOS to Aero compute board <https://github.com/intel-aero/meta-intel-aero/wiki/02-Initial-setup#flashing-the-bios>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:39
#: 8de587d7833045298071fd62517d5abc
msgid "`Flash the OS image to the Aero compute board <https://github.com/intel-aero/meta-intel-aero/wiki/02-Initial-setup#flash-intel-aero-linux-distribution>`__ using a USB thumb drive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:40
#: 00d8ec156d934f35b1e921cecbf7ae77
msgid "`Upgrade the FPGA <https://github.com/intel-aero/meta-intel-aero/wiki/02-Initial-setup#flashing-the-fpga>`__ using a .jam file included on the OS image"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:42
#: 7fcf8a3e79a34d4ea978b697ad614faf
msgid "The final step is to copy the **arducopter.px4** firmware to the Aero compute board and then flash it to the flight board:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:44
#: b545d1258827447d96dede21bc94fc11
msgid "Download the latest aero-fc ArduPilot firmware from `firmware.ardupilot.org <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Copter/latest/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:45
#: 5aede861503145e0aca23c62fcf008c9
msgid "Copy the above firmware to the Aero compute board in much the same way the BIOS's .rpm file was copied"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:46
#: 6bb6e359ed9b49728507c82663ed0c0f
msgid "`Flash the autopilot board <https://github.com/intel-aero/meta-intel-aero/wiki/02-Initial-setup#flashing-the-flight-controller-rtf-only>`__ with the **ardupilot.px4** firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:48
#: d31a282ed5dd44e2bca58bb8dc32b318
msgid "If you are developing ArduPilot, you can flash directly from the command line after compiling. Refer to `Build instructions <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/BUILD.md>`__ for more detailed instructions, but it's basically the following commands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:50
#: 05bf2aa8ced644ef99053ab7ea0b4bea
msgid "./waf configure --board aerofc-v1 ./waf copter --upload"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:54
#: 8545704baded4f888b950f8afc902301
msgid "Connecting and configuring with a ground station"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:56
#: e03f77d8ed054dcb905a77c3f3d9b21a
msgid "Connect a LiPo battery to the vehicle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:57
#: 0da98690911c45cc802ceac4f41ce9ea
msgid "Turn on the vehicle by pushing the \"Power\" button found between the two rear arms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:58
#: a65faec217324acda5ca0f792591bd3e
msgid "From your PC, connect to the vehicle's wifi access point (normally starts with \"Aero-\"), the default password is \"1234567890\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:59
#: 70ee759aa1414496891108fc2c13ef36
msgid "Start the ground station (i.e. mission planner), select \"UDP\" from the connection type and press \"Connect\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:60
#: 409cd65f3d184aba816fe72c957aa5b8
msgid "The default parameter file can be uploaded from the Mission Planner's Full Parameter Tree screen (raw parameter file is `here <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/Tools/Frame_params/intel-aero-rtf.param>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:65
#: 2cd80c6071344111b82e6451febad560
msgid "regular :ref:`compass <common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner>`, :ref:`Radio <common-radio-control-calibration>`, :ref:`accelerometer calibration <common-accelerometer-calibration>` is required (:ref:`ESC calibration <esc-calibration>` is not required)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:68
#: 6f6b650626074c51877d370a578ed5d5
msgid "Connecting the Transmitter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:70
#: f3bbb285634c463fba91ed57d60f8349
msgid "The transmitter that comes with the RTF is an off the shelf DSM-X DXe and a SPM4648 receiver, which is of autobind mode. The transmitter should always be powered on before the receiver (which is normally powered together with the vehicle).  If powered on after the vehicle it won't connect.  To overcome this you can simply disconnect the cable from the receiver, or go through the binding process, which involves powering on the transmitter while holding the \"BIND/PANIC/TRAINER\" button pressed. More information about the binding and connection can be found on the `receiver documentation <https://www.horizonhobby.com/pdf/SPM4648-Manual-EN.pdf>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:73
#: 382a321449ed471b81110475b6625eda
msgid "Known Issues with the Transmitter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:75
#: 0e4e7c9b825b4d9cb8229fb0a82b88e1
msgid "the \"MOTOR/THROW\" switch on the back-right of the transmitter should always be left in the \"ARM\" position or the throttle value sent to the vehicle will be too low"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:76
#: 7f522e2da62a49b0a8eb48a0e9385ec5
msgid "the \"FLAP\" switch is connected to Ch7 so it can be used as an auxiliary switch but position \"0\" is actually On, \"2\" is off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:77
#: 52b5ea56662b45f895f5879d4a7b1052
msgid "\"AUX\" and \"RATE\" switches are not configured to have any effect"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:79
#: 434232df8cb64f1ea46e1e2c60c80d06
msgid "The last three issues mentioned above could be resolved by reprogramming the transmitter using a `Spektrum TX/RX USB Programming Cable <https://www.spektrumrc.com/Products/Default.aspx?ProdID=SPMA3065>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:82
#: 2eeab93f23894e64ae1990e469c5fc5f
msgid "Improving the vehicle's center of gravity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:87
#: e4ec2310978c4e33a9d56533aa20095a
msgid "In the default configuration the vehicle is tail heavy but its center of gravity can be improved by shifting the battery forward. Either attach the battery to the underside of the vehicle (instead of between the upper and lower platforms) or remove one of the blue pillars as shown above."
msgstr ""

